                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                        "entry_id": "39c58581-493b-3b71-9745-02a4c30b9687",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die niet meer door andere geaccepteerd wordt en die in slechte omstandigheden verkeert"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7383d16-1ac2-463e-aaaf-5df2bae56f99",
                                "sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                                "text": "Afscheid van vrijplaats voor verschoppelingen: De Rotterdamse Pauluskerk gaat na de zomer tegen de vlakte. ‘Drugsdominee’ Hans Visser gaat niet lang erna met pensioen. Ruim een kwart eeuw lang zette hij de kerkdeur open voor verslaafden, hoeren, illegalen en alle anderen die nergens welkom waren. ‘Soms denk ik somber: ‘ik heb alles verloren.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3eeb540a-b2ab-452e-9b6b-76fbb25e6d57",
                                "sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                                "text": "Wat Europa nodig heeft is een herbezinning op zijn innerlijke waarden, een herformulering van zijn ideologie waarin alle aangesloten landen zich kunnen vinden. Dan pas zal Europa ook innerlijk een hechte gemeenschap kunnen worden die een adequate oplossing zal weten te vinden voor al die verschoppelingen die, om wat voor reden dan ook, langs zijn grenzen binnenstromen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76140d39-a96d-44bd-9a6d-1ab571dc9bfe",
                                "sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                                "text": "Eig dook in de archieven en stuitte op „vier verschoppelingen die iets controversieels deden, iets illegaals”, zegt hij in een interview via Skype. Zijn boek The birth of the Pill kwam deze week in Nederland uit als De man die seks uitvond, een titel die geen recht doet aan de drie anderen die volgens Eig aan de wieg stonden van de pil. „Ze waren alle vier nodig. Als een van hen het had opgegeven, was de pil er niet gekomen.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a1a604b-a900-4787-8e46-2afb50b536b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "39c58581-493b-3b71-9745-02a4c30b9687",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                        "target_lang_word": "outcast",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "outcast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c7b6019-1dae-3233-9f43-9f2b7c68377d",
                                        "entry_id": "1922064f-fa7a-3145-b0ce-60ddefb41e6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cast out; to banish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fcdc0ce-0e24-4609-8e19-798cf0e13180",
                                                "sense_id": "0c7b6019-1dae-3233-9f43-9f2b7c68377d",
                                                "text": "And her faire yellow locks behind her flew, / Looſely diſperſt with puff of euery blaſt: / All as a blazing ſtarre doth farre outcaſt / His hearie beames, and flaming lockes diſpredd, / At ſight whereof the people ſtand aghaſt: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f20995f4-f31f-4220-bb47-020e9b6f856c",
                                                "sense_id": "0c7b6019-1dae-3233-9f43-9f2b7c68377d",
                                                "text": "It means equal ruin to me, as the world reckons it — outcasting, the loss of my appointment, the breaking off my life's work. I pay my price."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "outcast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b154b2c-dbf3-3c99-9954-a26ee4fc9f13",
                                        "entry_id": "3315f9dd-599f-36e7-a483-ae59f2e7d189",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That has been cast out; banished, ostracized."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7e33450-4b43-4f8e-8761-2b692b956bbc",
                                                "sense_id": "9b154b2c-dbf3-3c99-9954-a26ee4fc9f13",
                                                "text": "O, horrible fate! Outcast, rejected, / As one with pestilence infected!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3757b719-0a4d-4a16-b9b2-2db71c31bf71",
                                                "sense_id": "9b154b2c-dbf3-3c99-9954-a26ee4fc9f13",
                                                "text": "We were not a big huggie family so I was very, very encased in a little stay-away-from-me shell growing-up, and here I got to open up and feel safe and able to touch and hold and be able to be with another human being, which was really a big relief, a very positive part of my understanding of myself that I wasn't just this outcast evil outsider of everything."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "outcast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44d4edd8-5da3-38f3-9dae-90e3ea2b16f7",
                                        "entry_id": "d3c3e57d-020b-398b-a770-91221f63374d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One that has been excluded from a society or system, a pariah, a leper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00859b53-870b-497c-9404-2dd23f9417d5",
                                                "sense_id": "44d4edd8-5da3-38f3-9dae-90e3ea2b16f7",
                                                "text": "The other factions believe that those who are Factionless are nomads and outcasts. But they are actually a fully functioning community."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72b5aba4-e0d0-3d0e-8860-084a7bcb937a",
                                        "entry_id": "d3c3e57d-020b-398b-a770-91221f63374d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of outsider: someone who does not belong, a misfit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26ad113e-870c-4173-b8f9-c0c527b8ef7d",
                                                "sense_id": "72b5aba4-e0d0-3d0e-8860-084a7bcb937a",
                                                "text": "Do you ever feel like an outcast?\nYou don't have to fit into the format\nOh, but it's okay to be different\n'Cause baby, so am I"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "256ec6b3-1751-32c0-90e4-5bd8c8dd304e",
                                        "entry_id": "d3c3e57d-020b-398b-a770-91221f63374d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quarrel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71b3bac1-2eb5-3a37-9d89-565466b92a21",
                                        "entry_id": "d3c3e57d-020b-398b-a770-91221f63374d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The amount of increase in the bulk of grain during malting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "34e6d60e-c766-488d-a8c7-eace470d77ef",
                        "source_entry_id": "39c58581-493b-3b71-9745-02a4c30b9687",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                        "target_lang_word": "pariah",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pariah",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fb8e39f-a072-3ea4-8f28-ea8eaceb4dd1",
                                        "entry_id": "c3f38f3e-edb4-3fca-bb4c-4c610b54f5db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of outcast: A person despised and excluded by their family, community, or society, especially a member of the untouchable castes in Indian society."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86ba56ca-37db-451f-b601-61fa69fc9eb8",
                                                "sense_id": "7fb8e39f-a072-3ea4-8f28-ea8eaceb4dd1",
                                                "text": "What is this smoking that it should be considered a crime? I believe in my heart that women are jealous of it, as of a rival. They speak of it as of some secret, awful vice that seizes upon a man, and makes him a Pariah from genteel society."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86e0ca5a-5b5b-4429-bcf0-8016b2dc4f00",
                                                "sense_id": "7fb8e39f-a072-3ea4-8f28-ea8eaceb4dd1",
                                                "text": "I’m a pariah, outlawed from Time Lord society."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad771975-d037-4101-b08a-19c9e664f8c4",
                                                "sense_id": "7fb8e39f-a072-3ea4-8f28-ea8eaceb4dd1",
                                                "text": "[…] I went from being a much-feted author to a pariah, since one of the many problems of being trashed on the front page of the New York Times is that everyone is in the know."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da89aa4b-9257-3d80-8ec0-24974a0c8444",
                                        "entry_id": "c3f38f3e-edb4-3fca-bb4c-4c610b54f5db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A similarly despised group of people or species of animal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9ee605c-d8f3-45dd-b598-368cdf83c75e",
                                                "sense_id": "da89aa4b-9257-3d80-8ec0-24974a0c8444",
                                                "text": "As ecological conditions became unfavorable for pig raising, there was no alternative function which could redeem its existence. The creature became not only useless, but worse than useless—harmful, a curse to touch or merely to see—a pariah animal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ab014ec-9269-478a-a72c-42ebafd772b9",
                                                "sense_id": "da89aa4b-9257-3d80-8ec0-24974a0c8444",
                                                "text": "This scenario could lead to war crimes the scale of which has not been seen in Europe since the Nazis — crimes that would make Vladimir Putin, his cronies and Russia as a country all global pariahs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4660e2e6-4dcf-3e86-a95b-952144c6cba7",
                                        "entry_id": "c3f38f3e-edb4-3fca-bb4c-4c610b54f5db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of pariah dog (“an Indian breed, any stray dog in Indian contexts”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9c36b0ee-e697-414c-a86e-017ba60c5792",
                        "source_entry_id": "39c58581-493b-3b71-9745-02a4c30b9687",
                        "source_sense_id": "2f051799-4b1a-3572-8a9f-fa2a0024e052",
                        "target_lang_word": "paria",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paria",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db0359fc-3f76-3a1b-8d68-f7df48777f31",
                                        "entry_id": "a25b742f-41f0-3f13-bfa0-621aca8b071d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Propio de, relativo o perteneciente a los linajes fuera del sistema de castas tradicional de la India, excluídos generalmente de la vida social y los oficios prestigiosos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "noun"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39c56cbf-9a11-4977-adab-ba334681ff1a",
                                                "sense_id": "db0359fc-3f76-3a1b-8d68-f7df48777f31",
                                                "text": "Aquí se ve al paria de la India despreciado hasta el extremo de considerarle inferior a los brutos, estándole prohibido todo contacto con los demás hombres, pues se creía que su maldita sombra contaminaba el agua y los demás alimentos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbbf5e5a-abe4-4c0b-8df1-0d621fae36ab",
                                                "sense_id": "db0359fc-3f76-3a1b-8d68-f7df48777f31",
                                                "text": "al cabo de siglo y medio de explotación de los pueblos coloniales y semicoloniales, las diferencias entre un obrero y su patrón fueron menos grandes que las existentes entre ese mismo obrero y un paria hindú o un peón boliviano."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "546ad1e1-6f23-3abc-946f-f1bfc33520cc",
                                        "entry_id": "a25b742f-41f0-3f13-bfa0-621aca8b071d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Por extensión, propio de, relativo o perteneciente a un grupo cualquier al que se excluye o margina de la sociedad."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "noun"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6388999c-7671-45ca-a5f5-ab9e0431c95e",
                                                "sense_id": "546ad1e1-6f23-3abc-946f-f1bfc33520cc",
                                                "text": "siempre amó, calló y sufrió en mi presencia, como un paria ante un Dios, como un eunuco ante la sultana, como un esclavo ante su dueño."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6805bc82-c5e8-4385-a2a3-e218c6689bc3",
                                                "sense_id": "546ad1e1-6f23-3abc-946f-f1bfc33520cc",
                                                "text": "jamás, jamás hubo para aquel sér desventurado una caricia o una sonrisa; él era el paria, el réprobo, el condenado irredimible."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "paria",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86796c3c-1ae7-38cb-b729-331e99ead549",
                                        "entry_id": "14c202f9-873e-310a-a40a-9e76ebe8909f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Forma del femenino singular de pario."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5fbcda1-a487-4ea3-8935-551ffd09af84",
                                                "sense_id": "86796c3c-1ae7-38cb-b729-331e99ead549",
                                                "text": "La primera referencia explícita a la paternidad simonídea de la invención —que ningún autor antiguo rechazó— se encuentra en la Crónica Paria, tablilla de mármol del año 264 a. C. aproximadamente, hallada en Paros en el siglo XVIII."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
